=== Z-1. what contrast the test can see ===
block A column: background 254, darkest 0, 254 levels (full pen)
attenuated copies of THAT SAME COLUMN, same method, same cuts:

contrast of the copy                  <90  <110  <130  <150  <170  <190  <215
as drawn, 254 levels (block A)         47    47    47    47    46    40    23   SEEN
circled mark, 146 levels                0    37    45    47    47    47    47   SEEN
vial-19 level, 110 levels               0     0     0    39    46    47    46   SEEN
80 levels                               0     0     0     0     0    46    47   SEEN
60 levels                               0     0     0     0     0     0    47   SEEN
45 levels                               0     0     0     0     0     0    44   SEEN
35 levels                               0     0     0     0     0     0     0   BLIND
25 levels                               0     0     0     0     0     0     0   BLIND
rifle-16 level, 19 levels               0     0     0     0     0     0     0   BLIND

(42 glyphs are known to be present in every row above: the ONLY thing changed
 is ink depth. A row of near-zeros is the test failing to see them.)

The floor has an exact cause: the sweep's top cut is <215 and this column's
background is 254, so the test can only see ink that reaches 254-215 = 39 levels
deep. 45 levels -> darkest 209, visible. 35 levels -> darkest 219, invisible.
The rifle-receiver mark in this same image is 19 levels (REPORT 6 item 6), so a
block drawn below this floor is not a hypothetical.

R1 observed, for comparison:        8     8     7     7    13    11     5
